      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- House of Thule, Lower Floors [zone=748]\n**Who:**\n- Researcher Breoro [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/8**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 8 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Related Zones:**\n- House of Thule: Welcome to My Nightmare [zone=761]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Keeper Barja [npc=36154]\n- Keeper Bianoa [npc=36147]\n- Keeper Cilkian [npc=36152]\n- Keeper Dalmari [npc=36148]\n- Keeper Eteran [npc=36151]\n- Keeper Jilam [npc=36153]\n- Keeper Moian [npc=36158]\n- Keeper Nujoi [npc=36155]\n- Keeper Polyai [npc=36149]\n- Keeper Tyoan [npc=36156]\n- Keeper Viljan [npc=36150]\n- Keeper Zilkan [npc=36157]\n- Researcher Breoro [npc=36161]\n- The Beast of Horror [npc=36166]\n- The Beast of Rage [npc=36165]\n- The Beast of Rot [npc=36162]\n- The Beast of the Unknown [npc=36164]\n- an ornate chest - Welcome to My Nightmare [npc=36167]\n**Related Quests:**\n- The Beast of Horror [quest=5120]\n- The Beast of Rage [quest=5121]\n- The Beast of Rot [quest=5122]\n- The Beast of the Unknown [quest=5123]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Oct 21 19:33:24 2010\nModified: Mon Feb 25 01:08:05 2019 | | _This is a group progression task that begins with Researcher Breoro in the lower floors of the House of Thule (just inside the front door). The task locks after killing the last mini-boss, regardless of order._\n_You must have completed his four solo tasks prior to being able to request this one._\nYou say, 'Hail, Researcher Breoro'\nResearcher Breoro says 'Now that all of the potions have been brewed, it is time to take on the beasts themselves. This will be no easy [task]. Or, just in case, you can retrieve more ingredients for me, so I can brew another [potion of rot], [potion of rage], [potion of horror], or [potion of the unknown].'\nYou say, 'What task?'\nResearcher Breoro says 'Once I drink these potions, you will be able to enter my nightmare and destroy the beasts. Each beast has three protectors that will need to be defeated before the beasts themselves can be confronted. When you are [ready], I will drink the potions.'\nYou say, 'We're ready'\nResearcher Breoro says 'I have consumed the potions and can already begin to feel their effect on me. Please let me know when you are ready to [go], and you will be able to enter my nightmare and hopefully end this once and for all.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Welcome to My Nightmare'.\nDefeat the necromancers guarding the Beasts of Rot, Horror, Rage, and the Unknown. Once you have accomplished this, speak with Researcher Breoro.\nYou say, 'Let's go'\nResearcher Breoro says 'May the Gods be with you.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered House of Thule: Breoro's Nightmare.\n\n---\n\n_The first task steps open are all the \"Destroy Keeper...\" steps. These Keepers are found in groups of three in the same locations where you'd find the \"beastling\" mobs in the non-instanced zone._\n_Killing each group of Keepers spawns the Beast associated with them. The Beasts spawn right on top of the corpse of the last Keeper to die in each set._\n_Keepers hit for a max ~6,000 and are stunnable, rootable/snareable, mezzable, and able to be harmonized._\n_The Beasts hit for a max ~8,500, enrage, have more hitpoints, and are immune to crowd control methods. They also each come with an AE debuff (listed below). These debuffs are triggered by using same-resist spells against them (The Beast of Rot's debuff, for example, would be triggered by any disease-based spell used against it)._\n_The Researcher at the end hits for a max ~8,000 and also has a lot of hitpoints._\nDestroy Keeper Bianoa 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Dalmari 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Polyai 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy the Beast of Rot 0/1 (House of Thule)\nThe Beast of Rot senses that you would make a good meal and closes in for the attack!\nCurse of Rot: PB AE 400', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Incoming Spell Damage by 20%\n2: Limit: Resist (Disease allowed)\n3: Increase Disease Counter by 50\nRot Breath: Single Target, Disease (-700)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 23000\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 6000 per tick\n3: Increase Disease Counter by 40\nDestroy Keeper Viljan 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Eteran 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Cilkian 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy the Beast of the Unknown 0/1 (House of Thule)\nThe Beast of the Unknown swiftly approaches.\nCurse of Fire: PB AE 400', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Incoming Spell Damage by 20%\n2: Limit: Resist (Fire allowed)\n3: Increase Curse Counter by 50\nDark Embrace: Single Target, Fire (-700)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 20000 per tick _(1 tick)_\n2: Blindness (1)\nDestroy Keeper Jilam 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Barja 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Nujoi 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy the Beast of Horror 0/1 (House of Thule)\nThe Beast of Horror skitters towards you, eager to end your life.\nCurse of Poison: PB AE 400', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Incoming Spell Damage by 20%\n2: Limit: Resist (Poison allowed)\n3: Increase Poison Counter by 50\nNightmarish Venom: Single Target, Poison (-700)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 8000 per tick\n2: Decrease Mana by 5000 per tick\n3: Decrease Endurance by 800 per tick\n4: Increase Poison Counter by 30\nDestroy Keeper Tyoan 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Zilkan 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy Keeper Moian 0/1 (House of Thule)\nDestroy the Beast of Rage 0/1 (House of Thule)\nThe Beast of Rage becomes enraged and rushes to the attack!\nCurse of Frost: PB AE 400', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Incoming Spell Damage by 20%\n2: Limit: Resist (Cold allowed)\n3: Increase Curse Counter by 50\nIcy Blow: Single Target, Cold (-700)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 30000\n2: Stun (5.00 sec)\nSpeak with Researcher Breoro 0/1 (House of Thule)\nYou say, 'Hail, Researcher Breoro'\nResearcher Breoro says 'I can no longer feel the presence of the beasts. Thanks to you fools, I am now able to control my nightmare and have more power than I could have ever imagined. Your services will no longer be needed.'\nDefend yourself against Researcher Breoro 0/1 (House of Thule)\n_Researcher Breoro hits for a max ~8,000, has 650,000 hitpoints, and casts a standard set of wizard spells._\n_He also procs the spell \"Dream Splinter\" on his target:_\nDream Splinter: Magic (-650)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 15000\n_As his health approaches 0%, he goes inactive._\nStop! Stop fighting! This is madness! We must stop this at once!\nSpeak with Researcher Breoro 0/1 (House of Thule)\nResearcher Breoro says 'I don't know what came over me. I am truly sorry. I could not resist the rush of power dangled before my eyes. Let me know when you are ready to [leave] this place.'\nCollect your reward from the ornate chest 0/1 (House of Thule)\n_An ornate chest spawns nearby with loot._\n\n---\n\n_Task Rewards:_\nExperience (about 6% regular exp at Level 86 or 4 AAs worth)\n315 platinum\n20 Dream Motes\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n_Known chest rewards (1 item + 1 spell per task):_\nAcorn of Spite\nAxe of the Woodcutter\nDeathpoint\nGanborn's Rod of Curses\nHardened Dragon's Tear\nJagged Metal Knuckles\nRing of Restless Sleep\nRing of the Fearborn\nSlippery Slimerock\nTerror Infused Linked Vambraces\nMinor Nebulous Dream Fragment\nLesser Nebulous Dream Fragment\nMedian Nebulous Dream Fragment\nGreater Nebulous Dream Fragment\nGlowing Nebulous Dream Fragment",
    },
