      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- House of Thule, Upper Floors [zone=753]\n**Who:**\n- Abbit Scribbletch [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/2**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 2 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 90\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Factions Raised:**\n- Dream Delvers +?\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Argan's Memoir [item=92742]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Keega [npc=36297]\n- Khalis [npc=36314]\n- a protective imp [npc=36313]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Morzad Chronicle - Abbit's Betrayal (#2) [quest=5198]\n- Morzad Chronicle - Dead or Alive or Other (#4) [quest=5200]\n- Morzad Chronicle - Never Trust a Morzad (#3) [quest=5199]\n- Morzad Chronicle - The Morzad Confrontation (#5) [quest=5201]\n**Era:** | !House of Thule\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 8 23:31:00 2010\nModified: Sat Oct 22 20:55:41 2011 | | _This task is the first in a series of five that begins with Abbit Scribbletch, a gnome found in the first room on the left immediately on entering the northeastern wing of the House of Thule's Upper Floors._\nYou say, 'Hail, Abbit Scribbletch'\nAbbit Scribbletch says 'I cannot believe this has [happened]. I should know better than to trust a source with whom I do not normally deal with. But I was so close!'\nYou say, 'What happened?'\nAbbit Scribbletch says 'I am a collector, of many things, but books are my main passion. I was so close, or so I thought, to finding the lost memoirs of the [Morzad] leader Argan. '\nYou say, 'Who are the Morzad?'\nAbbit Scribbletch says 'It makes sense that you've never heard of the Morzad. They were an underground group of explorers and archeologists who sought powerful relics in order to gain more power for themselves. No one really knew to what end. The Morzad were thought to have vanished after [Argan] was killed by Cazic Thule himself.'\nYou say, 'Who's Argan?'\nAbbit Scribbletch says 'I was getting to that! Argan made note of every relic the Morzad ever found and kept in a book along with its location. The book has come to be known as Argan's Memoir. This is why I am here. I thought I had good information that the book was here, but as soon as I arrived, I have been plagued by attackers. I am a collector, not a combatant! And now I am stuck here it seems. Will you [help] me?'\nYou say, 'I'll help you'\nAbbit Scribbletch says 'Excellent! I was to meet someone named Keega here. You must find him and talk to him in my stead. But you must hurry. I am sure he has been waiting for me, but I have been unable to move. '\nYou have been assigned the task 'Morzad Chronicle - Argan's Memoir'.\nAbbit Scribbletch is stuck here while looking for Argan's Memoir. He has asked for your help in meeting the one who knows where the book can be found.\n\n---\n\nSpeak to Keega 0/1 (House of Thule, Upper Floors)\n_Keega is an Erudite found in the first hall of the northwestern wing._\nYou say, 'Hail, Keega'\nKeega says 'You are not [Abbit]!'\nYou say, 'Abbit sent me...'\nKeega says 'Very well... The book he seeks is being held by an imp who calls himself Khalis. He is especially annoying. But it shouldn't take much to get the book from him. He seems to not know, or care, what it is.'\nKill 2 protective imps 0/2 (House of Thule, Upper Floors)\n_To get to Khalis and his protective imps, keep going through the northwestern wing until you come to the rotdog room. From there, go south and through that hall to Khalis' room._\n_Note: The protective imps used to be triggered spawns by hailing Keega. A patch changed them to regular spawns, so they'll always be up next to Khalis (unless someone's very recently killed them)._\n_Khalis is not aggro, but the imps are as well as a number of undead in the room. They each hit for a max ~6,500._\na protective imp says 'I will pry those pretty little eyes from your skull and feast like a king upon your every fleshy nerve!'\na protective imp has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na protective imp's corpse says 'Oops! Back to The Faceless I go. I'll be back, and your eyes will be mine!'\nSpeak to Khalis 0/1 (House of Thule, Upper Floors)\nYou say, 'Hail, Khalis'\nKhalis says 'What have we here? How do I know? Quiet, let me talk! What book? You know what book! Ah, that book! I will give you the book. But first, you must answer something for me. What can burn but is not fire, and has a way of destroying rationality? '\nAnswer Khalis' riddle 0/1 (House of Thule, Upper Floors)\nYou say, 'Hate'\nKhalis says 'Correct! I don't get it? Hush! It was too easy! You have answered correctly, so here is the book.'\n_You receive Argan's Memoir._\nDeliver Argan's Memoir to Abbit Scribbletch 0/1 (House of Thule, Upper Floors)\n_On hand-in:_\nYour task 'Morzad Chronicle - Argan's Memoir' has been updated.\nAbbit Scribbletch says 'I cannot believe you retrieved it, and so easily! Thank you.'\nYou have found the book that in which Abbit was looking.\nYour faction standing with Dream Delvers got better.\n_Rewards:_\n158 platinum\nExperience\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n15 Dream Motes\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]",
